[{"id":"smq-year2-2.05-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>State the period of each of the following functions:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\sin(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\cos(4\\pi x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\tan(\\pi x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\sin(\\frac\\pi2x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\cos(\\frac\\pi4x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\tan(\\frac\\pi2x-\\frac\\pi4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi}{52}x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\cos(\\frac{2\\pi}7x+\\frac\\pi{18})\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi}{365}(x-30))\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\cos(\\frac\\pi{26}(x+7))\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\\div1=2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\\div4\\pi=\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi\\div\\pi=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\\div\\frac\\pi2=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\\div\\frac\\pi4=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi\\div\\frac\\pi2=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">g)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\\div\\frac{2\\pi}{52}=52\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">h)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\\div\\frac{2\\pi}7=7\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">i)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\\div\\frac{2\\pi}{365}=365\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">j)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\\div\\frac\\pi{26}=52\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.05-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>In each of the following cases, the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has been stretched parallel to the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p><p>State the equation of each curve.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.05/questions/assets/diagrams/205-q2a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.05/questions/assets/diagrams/205-q2b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.05/questions/assets/diagrams/205-q2c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.05/questions/assets/diagrams/205-q2d.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}7x\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}1x\\right)=\\sin(2\\pi x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{600}x\\right)=\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi{300}x\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{24}x\\right)=\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi{12}x\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.05-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>All the following graphs are transformations of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>State the equation of each:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.05/questions/assets/diagrams/205-q3a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.05/questions/assets/diagrams/205-q3b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.05/questions/assets/diagrams/205-q3c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.05/questions/assets/diagrams/205-q3d.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{13}x\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}1x\\right)=2\\sin(2\\pi x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=10\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{20}x\\right)=10\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi{10}x\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-5\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{30}x\\right)=-5\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi{15}x\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.05-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>State the amplitude of each of the following periodic functions:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin(3\\pi x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4+\\cos(\\pi x+0.1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=55+12\\sin(\\pi x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1-2\\sin(x+\\frac\\pi2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.05-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>For each of the following functions state the minimum and maximum of the function:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin(2\\pi x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3+\\cos(\\pi x-\\frac\\pi2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=14+6\\sin(30\\pi x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2-7\\cos(\\frac\\pi2x+0.2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Max is 1, min is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Max is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3+1=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, min is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3-1=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Max is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"14+6=20\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, min is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"14-6=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Max is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2+7=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, min is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2-7=-5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.05-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>All the following graphs are all the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=a+b\\sin(cx)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>In each case, find the equation of the graph:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.05/questions/assets/diagrams/205-q6a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.05/questions/assets/diagrams/205-q6b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.05/questions/assets/diagrams/205-q6c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.05/questions/assets/diagrams/205-q6d.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Period: 10</p>","<p>Amplitude: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{5-1}2=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Translate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\3\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=3+2\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{10}x\\right)=3+2\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi5x\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Period: 30</p>","<p>Amplitude: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{2.5-1.5}2=\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Translate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\2\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=2+\\tfrac12\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{30}x\\right)=2+\\tfrac12\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi{15}x\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Period: 20</p>","<p>Amplitude: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{2-(-4)}2=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Translate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-1+3\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{20}x\\right)=-1+3\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi{10}x\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Period: 7</p>","<p>Amplitude: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{25-15}2=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Translate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\20\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=20-5\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}7x\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.05-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>The river Hamble is tidal. On one day the depth of the Hamble oscillates between a maximum of 3.6 metres at 8:00 am and a minimum of 2.0 metres at 10:30 pm. Kaelen decides to model the depth of the river, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres by the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d=a+b\\cos\\left(\\frac25\\pi t\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of hours since 8:00 am.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>State the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> that Kaelen should use.</p></li><li><p>State the period of this equation.</p></li><li><p>Calculate the total time, according to this model, that the Hamble is less than 2.5 metres in depth within the first 7 hours.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Max -- min <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"=3.6-2=1.6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{1.6}2=0.8\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d=2.8+0.8\\cos\\left(\\frac25\\pi t\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=2.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=0.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Period is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{2\\pi}{\\frac25\\pi}=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2.8+0.8\\cos\\left(\\frac25\\pi t\\right)=2.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Find the first value:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac25\\pi t=\\arccos(-0.375)=1.95519310129\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Find the second value:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2\\pi-1.95519310129\\ldots=4.32799220589\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac25\\pi t=4.32799220589\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=1.556\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=3.444\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Add on the period: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.556+5=6.556\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Time below 2.5 metres:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(3.444-1.556)+(7-6.556)=2.332\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>2 hours 20 minutes</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.05-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>The temperature, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T^\\circ\\mathrm C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of an average human can be modelled by the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"T=36.8-0.64\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi{12}(h+2)\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of hours since midnight.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the maximum temperature of an average human.</p></li><li><p>Find the first time at which this maximum occurs after midnight.</p></li></ol><p>The temperature, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T^\\circ\\mathrm C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of an average dog varies between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"38.3^\\circ\\mathrm C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"39.2^\\circ\\mathrm C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li><p>Find an equation to model a dog's temperature of the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=a-b\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi{12}(h+2)\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=36.8+0.64=37.44^\\circ\\mathrm C\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>First time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi{12}(h+2)\\right)=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac\\pi{12}(h+2)=\\frac{3\\pi}2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h+2=18\\Rightarrow h=16\\text{ hours}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore 16:00</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Max -- min is: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"39.2-38.3=0.9\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{0.9}2=0.45,\\qquad38.3+0.45=38.75\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"T=38.75-0.45\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi{12}(h+2)\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.05-q9","number":9,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite Knowledge for Q9: Graph Transformations (combinations)</strong> The time of sunset, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hours for the first day of the week <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for a year may be modelled by the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t=18.5+2.4\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{52}(x+26)\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq x\\leq52\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Describe the transformations which map</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t=\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{52}(x+26)\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>onto</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t=18.5+2.4\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{52}(x+26)\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Find the time of the sunset in the 14th week of the year.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Stretch parallel to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis, scale factor 2.4</p>","<p>Translate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\18.5\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=14\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t=18.5+2.4\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{52}(14+26)\\right)=16.1174987\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Time of sunset is 16:07</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.05-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>The number of passengers waiting on a platform for a train is recorded over the course of a day, and they are plotted on a graph. Passengers are only counted once as they embark on a train before the next count of passengers takes place.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.05/questions/assets/diagrams/205-q10.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>It is believed that the data can be modelled with the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"N=140+120\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi6(t-3)\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of passengers on the platform and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of hours after midnight. According to the model, find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the difference in the number of passengers between 5 am and 9 am</p></li><li><p>the times at which the total number of passengers on the platform is over 200 over the 24-hour period.</p></li><li><p>Explain why it may not be suitable to use this function to model the data.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"N=140+120\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi6(5-3)\\right)=243.923\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"N=140+120\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi6(9-3)\\right)=140\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"243.923\\ldots-140=104\" data-display=\"false\"></span> passengers</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"140+120\\sin\\left(\\frac\\pi6(t-3)\\right)=200\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Find the first value:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac\\pi6(t-3)=\\arcsin(0.5)=\\frac\\pi6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Find the second value: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi-\\frac\\pi6=\\frac{5\\pi}6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>The period is: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\\div\\frac\\pi6=12\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Add on the period: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=4+12=16\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=8+12=20\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Times at which 200 passengers: 04:00, 08:00, 16:00, 20:00</p>","<p>04:00 to 08:00, and 16:00 to 20:00</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>The number of passengers is a discrete number which is then being represented by a continuous curve. It also assumes the same pattern outside of the data collection times, so for example, the model says the platform is never empty and that there are symmetries around the times when there are a maximum number of passengers, so it predicts the same number of passengers at both 2am and 10am which seems unrealistic!</p>"]}]